// RULE: T-Money-Add / W7, in return position. A signature is a claim about what the
// function yields, and a currency is part of what it yields.
// WHY IT MATTERS: the `let` position and the call position were the two the checker looked
// at. A function whose body yields `Money<eur>` under a `-> Money<usd>` signature launders
// the currency at the *callee's* boundary instead, and every caller then reasons about a
// `Money<usd>` that never existed — the same defect, one indirection away.
// EXPECT: NL0332
// STAGE: check
fn fee() -> Money<usd> ! { } { 1.50 eur }
